CREATING AN EXAM STRUCTURE ---------------------------------------------- 

	Select an exam from the 'All Available Exams' JList sequentially (first Exam 1, then Exam 2, etc.). Then, 
	click "Create An Exam" to create an exam structure. Creating an exam structure does three things. First, it 
	initially populates four (4) tables with one or more ArrayLists (listOfQuestionsSER) holding null values 
	that will eventually be populated with created anonymous QuestionSuper objects. Second, it inserts an 
	outerMasterListOfMastersSER into the 5th table, STUDENTS_OUTERNESTED_TABLE4 where final graded exams 
	are stored. This outer initially holds ten (10) ArrayList<ArrayList<QuestionSuper>> masterListOfQuestionsSER 
	objects only (one per exam). And third, an outerMasterListOfMastersSER is inserted into DISPLAY_EXAMS_QUESTIONS_TABLE_1, 
	with 10 (or fewer) null values instead of 10 masterListOfQuestionsSER objects like in the STUDENTS_OUTERNESTED_TABLE4. 
	
	When you first create an exam you will be asked for the number of questions you wish to begin with. If you choose, 
	say, one, then the first null will be a masterListOfQuestionsSER containing a listOfQuestionsSER of null values, 
	depending on the number of questions you chose. For each question added to a masterListOfQuestionsSER exam, an initial 
	listOfQuestionsSER is added - with a null value per question. Remember, in this DISPLAY_EXAMS_QUESTIONS_TABLE_1, 
	accessed through the DisplayExamsAndQuestions class, each exam (masterListOfQuestionsSER) only contains 
	one listOfQuestionsSER, never more. 	
	
