WHY NO UML CHART?  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	
	This Swing app was built in Eclipse using WindowBuilder. The main class is BrainBuilder3.java which displays the GUI, and 
	roughly 3,300 lines of code are contained within the constructor. It's a one-way-street of sorts. From what I can 
	tell, outside classes/objects can be accessed from within that constructor and used, but instances of those 
	numerous classes cannot access, say, the text fields etc., within that BrainBuilder3 constructor; 
	and I tried .... After all, how do you get inside the constructor while it is in the process of 
	being constructed? Accordingly, a UML chart would consist of BrainBuilder3 at the top, with a 
	spaghetti-string cluster of lines extending below connecting the many classes it utilizes, with 
	interconnecting lines between the roughly 37 classes (not including the many 
	anonymous QuestionSuper subclasses). But feel free to try. 

